    lines+=['','Complete per-history/aggregate comparator and seed metrics, per-person losses, evidence/weight distributions, bootstrap intervals and numerical checks are in the realization JSON files. Losses and squared contrast errors are averaged across histories; probabilities are not pooled. No control or pooled result rescues an ES failure.','',f'Execution: {counts}. Verification: {v.get("comparisons",0)} exact comparison operations; maximum discrepancy {v.get("max_abs")}. Each operation checks all elements of its frozen object. Private hashes checked before and after.','', 'Forward replay independently implements prediction matrix multiplication and a dense two-count DP, checking full optimizer slices, priors and mixtures. Metric replay uses a different loss reduction and multiplicity-weighted bootstrap; report schema, gates and much contrast logic are shared and are not an entirely independent statistical implementation.','', 'The .009 theorem bounds expected positive inactive excess loss over possible support responses under the correct known-base, fixed-label, independent-response model. It does not guarantee an observed cohort below .009 or .01 and does not guarantee active recovery. Both empirical point gates and theory checks are reported separately. Bootstrap intervals condition on the fitted heads and fixed histories; they exclude retraining and domain uncertainty.','',f'Resource accounting: {resources}.','', 'Preserve DICES/SRO exposure, v1 null failure, v2 bounded96-support qualification, and short-history primary failure. PR18 remains a distinct planning package; its CLI and seed banks were not used. Corpus production/review PR14/16 remain separate. Stop for review; do not retune E/F/G/H or merge.']
